  </metadata>
  <content>
  <note class="self-check"><para>Using a calculator, Joanna made the following table and then made the following conjecture: \(3x\) is always greater than \((1.02)^x\). Is Joanna correct? Explain.</para>
<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
  <tgroup cols="3"><tbody><row>
      <entry><emphasis>
        \(x\)
     </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        \((1.02)^x\)
     </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
        \(3x\)
     </emphasis></entry></row>
  <row>
      <entry>
        1
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1.02
      </entry>
      <entry>
        3
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        2
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1.0404
      </entry>
      <entry>
        6
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        3
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1.0612
      </entry>
      <entry>
        9
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        4
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1.0824
      </entry>
      <entry>
        12
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        5
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1.1041
      </entry>
      <entry>
        15
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody></tgroup></table>
</note>
</content>
</document>